Fixed.

The bug was in `src/sim.ts:43` in `advanceTurn`:

```ts
if (foodSurplus >= 0) {   // grew even at break-even
```

`foodSurplus` is `foodProduced - foodConsumed`. The `>= 0` condition let population grow whenever production merely matched consumption (surplus of 0), contradicting the docstring's "if there was a food surplus." Changed to `> 0` so population only grows on a genuine surplus.

Verified: `npm run test` passes (4/4) and `npm run typecheck` is clean.


